🚀 PERFORMANCE RULES
Parallelization Standards
# ✅ CORRECT: True parallelization with order preservation
class ProcessingService:
    async def process_large_dataset(self, items: List[Item]) -> List[Result]:
        # Rate limiting
        semaphore = asyncio.Semaphore(settings.max_concurrent)
        
        async def process_single_item(item: Item) -> Result:
            async with semaphore:
                return await expensive_operation(item)
        
        # True parallelization
        tasks = [process_single_item(item) for item in items]
        results = await asyncio.gather(*tasks)
        
        # Preserve order
        results.sort(key=lambda x: x.original_index)
        return results
Progress Tracking Rules
# ✅ CORRECT: Monotonic progress (never backwards)
class ProgressTracker:
    def __init__(self, total_items: int):
        self.total_items = total_items
        self.completed = 0
        self.lock = asyncio.Lock()
    
    async def increment(self):
        async with self.lock:  # Thread-safe
            self.completed += 1
            progress = self.completed / self.total_items
            await update_progress(progress)  # Always increasing
Performance Guidelines
Async/await for all I/O operations
Semaphores for rate limiting
Batch processing for efficiency
Concurrent operations where safe
Memory optimization for large datasets
Progress tracking must be monotonic
